{%- comment -%}
  Shared Quick View modal - ONE instance per page, rendered from
  layout/theme.liquid (gated to `template.suffix contains 'c5dla'`, same
  condition that already wraps `<main>` in `.c5dla-scope` for this template
  family - see that file's own comment). Rendered from the layout rather
  than from sections/5dla_collection-product-grid.liquid on purpose: that
  section (and therefore this snippet) can appear MULTIPLE times on one
  page (e.g. templates/page.c5dla-trisuits-4-hwr.json renders it 3x, once
  per card style) - rendering the modal from each instance would duplicate
  this markup's ids/aria wiring once per section instead of sharing one
  dialog, so it lives in the layout instead.

  Uses Bootstrap 5's own Modal component (https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/components/modal/,
  already a project dependency - collection.scss does a full
  `@import "bootstrap/scss/bootstrap"` and client/ver_2_0/js/collection.js
  already imports `bootstrap/js/dist/tab`) instead of a bespoke
  overlay/dialog pair: `.modal`/`.modal-dialog`/`.modal-content`/
  `.modal-header`/`.modal-body` are Bootstrap's own classes, so backdrop,
  Escape-to-close, body scroll lock, and focus trap/return all come from
  Bootstrap's `Modal` component for free (client/ver_2_0/js/modules/
  quick-view.js only calls `Modal.getOrCreateInstance(el).show()`/`.hide()`
  - see that file's own comment for why the image carousel still waits for
  Bootstrap's `shown.bs.modal` event before initializing).

  Content layout is ported from the legacy quick view template
  (snippets/site-template.liquid's `#quickiew-tempvlate` `<script>`, built
  by assets/wpbingo.js's `wpbingo.QuickView`) - same two-column shape
  (`.img-quickview` image area | info column with vendor/price/variants/
  quantity/add-to-cart/availability/full-details), using Bootstrap's own
  grid (`.row`/`.col-*`, already available via the full Bootstrap import
  above) for that layout instead of a custom CSS grid.

  One deliberate difference: the legacy template's image carousel
  (`.quickview-images`) is a Slick carousel (assets/wpbingo.js's
  `createImageCarousel`, `$(...).slick({fade:true, infinite:false, ...})`).
  Per request, this one uses Swiper instead (already a project dependency -
  see package.json) - `data-c5dla-quick-view-carousel`/`-carousel-wrapper`/
  `-carousel-prev`/`-carousel-next` below are a plain Swiper
  container/wrapper/nav-button shape (client/ver_2_0/js/modules/
  quick-view.js builds the `.swiper-slide`s and instantiates `Swiper` with
  the Navigation + EffectFade modules - same fade transition + prev/next
  arrows the legacy carousel had, swapped library).

  --- How to add a Quick View trigger to ANY snippets/5dla_product-card-*.liquid ---
  This modal and its JS don't know anything about a specific card variant's
  markup - they only need a trigger element anywhere on the page shaped
  like:

    <button
      type="button"
      class="quick-view-button"
      data-quick-view-trigger
      data-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
      data-variant-id="{{ current_variant.id }}"
    >
      {{ 'products.product.quickview' | t }}
    </button>

  - `data-quick-view-trigger` is the only REQUIRED hook - quick-view.js
    delegates a single document-level click listener for it, so a future
    card variant just needs this button in its markup; no JS changes, no
    re-init call, nothing else to wire up (new cards appended by
    pagination/AJAX re-render work automatically for the same reason - the
    listener isn't bound per-card).
  - `data-handle` (required) is the product handle - quick-view.js fetches
    `/products/<handle>.js` to populate the modal (this endpoint's `media`/
    `variants[].featured_media` is also what feeds the image carousel).
  - `data-variant-id` (optional) preselects that variant instead of the
    product's first available one - keep it live on variant change the same
    way snippets/5dla_product-card-3.liquid does (`dynamic="quick-view-trigger"`,
    updated by client/ver_2_0/js/modules/variant-state.js's
    `updateQuickViewTrigger`) if the card has its own variant picker.
  - If the trigger sits inside an element carrying `data-product-json`
    (card 3's `[data-variant-picker]` root), quick-view.js reads that
    inline JSON instead of fetching - an optional optimization, not
    required for a new card to work.
  - `class="quick-view-button"` is purely presentational (for per-card
    skinning/positioning); only the `data-quick-view-trigger` attribute is
    load-bearing for JS.

  Everything inside `[data-c5dla-quick-view-content]` below is populated by
  quick-view.js at open time - this file only provides the static shell.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div
  class="modal c5dla-quick-view"
  id="c5dlaQuickViewModal"
  data-c5dla-quick-view
  tabindex="-1"
  aria-labelledby="c5dla-quick-view-title"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" data-c5dla-quick-view-dialog>
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h2 class="modal-title" id="c5dla-quick-view-title" data-c5dla-quick-view-title></h2>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn-close"
          data-bs-dismiss="modal"
          aria-label="{{ 'products.facets.close' | t }}"
        ></button>
      </div>

      <div class="modal-body">
        <div class="c5dla-quick-view__loading" data-c5dla-quick-view-loading hidden>
          Loading...
        </div>

        <div class="c5dla-quick-view__content row" data-c5dla-quick-view-content hidden>
          <div class="col-12 col-md-6 c5dla-quick-view__media img-quickview">
            <div class="c5dla-quick-view__carousel swiper" data-c5dla-quick-view-carousel>
              <div class="swiper-wrapper" data-c5dla-quick-view-carousel-wrapper></div>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="c5dla-quick-view__carousel-nav c5dla-quick-view__carousel-nav--prev"
                data-c5dla-quick-view-carousel-prev
                aria-label="{{ 'products.zoom.prev' | t }}"
              >
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6"></path>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="c5dla-quick-view__carousel-nav c5dla-quick-view__carousel-nav--next"
                data-c5dla-quick-view-carousel-next
                aria-label="{{ 'products.zoom.next' | t }}"
              >
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"></path>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="col-12 col-md-6 c5dla-quick-view__info bwp-single-info">
            <a class="c5dla-quick-view__vendor" data-c5dla-quick-view-vendor href="#" hidden></a>
            <div class="c5dla-quick-view__price" data-c5dla-quick-view-price></div>

            <div class="c5dla-quick-view__options" data-c5dla-quick-view-options></div>

            <div
              class="c5dla-quick-view__available"
              data-c5dla-quick-view-available
              data-in-stock-label="{{ 'products.product.in_stock' | t }}"
              data-out-stock-label="{{ 'products.product.out_stock' | t }}"
            >
              <span data-c5dla-quick-view-available-text></span>
            </div>

            <form
              class="form-addtocart c5dla-quick-view__form"
              action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
              method="post"
              enctype="multipart/form-data"
              data-product-form
              data-c5dla-quick-view-form
            >
              <input type="hidden" name="id" value="" data-c5dla-quick-view-variant-input>

              <div class="c5dla-quick-view__quantity" data-c5dla-quick-view-quantity>
                <label class="c5dla-quick-view__quantity-label">{{ 'products.product.quantity' | t }}</label>
                <div class="c5dla-quick-view__qty-selector">
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="c5dla-quick-view__qty-btn"
                    data-c5dla-quick-view-qty-minus
                    aria-label="{{ 'cart.general.reduce_quantity' | t }}"
                  >&minus;</button>
                  <input
                    type="number"
                    name="quantity"
                    min="1"
                    value="1"
                    inputmode="numeric"
                    class="c5dla-quick-view__qty-input"
                    data-c5dla-quick-view-qty-input
                  >
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="c5dla-quick-view__qty-btn"
                    data-c5dla-quick-view-qty-plus
                    aria-label="{{ 'cart.general.increase_quantity' | t }}"
                  >+</button>
                </div>
              </div>

              <button
                type="submit"
                class="js-btn-addtocart button product-action button-dark"
                data-c5dla-quick-view-submit
                data-add-to-cart-label="{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}"
                data-sold-out-label="{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}"
              >
                <span data-c5dla-quick-view-submit-label>{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}</span>
              </button>
            </form>

            <a class="c5dla-quick-view__full-details" data-c5dla-quick-view-full-link href="#">
              {{ 'products.product.full_details' | t }}
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
